#! nix-shell -i python3 -p "python3.withPackages (ps: [ ps.requests ps.websockets ])"
"""dictbench — compare speech-to-text providers on your own read-aloud clips.

  dictbench record [--only N,M | --next N] [--session S]   read sentences.txt (else sentences.example.txt, or $DICTBENCH_SENTENCES) aloud, one clip each
  dictbench run [SESSION] [-p a,b] transcribe the latest (or named) session
  dictbench providers              list providers and whether a key was found

Audio is captured exactly like dictate: pw-record on the configured multichannel
source, then ffmpeg picks DICTATE_CHAN and resamples to 16 kHz mono. Clips and
reports live under ~/.local/state/dictate/bench, never in the repo.

Keys come from the environment or ~/.config/dictate/keys.env (KEY=value
lines): GROQ_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY,
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY.

Scores: WER on normalized words (lowercase, punctuation dropped, dotted names
like CLAUDE.md kept whole), term hits for glossary words that occur in the
reference, and latency. HTTP latency is the whole request after you stop
speaking; streaming latency is end-of-audio to final transcript, with audio
sent at real-time pace the way a live mic would.
"""
